{
  "_comment": [
    "The since-minor rule's verdict oracle (docs/VERSION_POLICY.md, \"What bumps",
    "what\", and the spec's validation rule 1). One file, two readers:",
    "conformance/test_member_since.py runs every row through the Python",
    "check_member_since and reference/cpp/tests through the C++ one, each with",
    "the row's own map, so the rule is measured while the real map is small.",
    "",
    "A row is a map (field, member, the minor that added it), the version a",
    "document declares, one member of one field, and the verdict: ok, or refuse",
    "(a data error the validator raises). The members here are invented on",
    "purpose; the rule must not depend on which members are real."
  ],
